<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/brick-ranch.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/brick-ranch-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/brick-ranch.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Southaven</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">North Mississippi</p><h1>Southaven and DeSoto County Claim Appraisal</h1><p class="lede">DeSoto County grew fast, and so did its roofs. When hail, straight-line wind or ice damages your Southaven home and the carrier’s estimate falls short, appraisal can settle the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>DeSoto County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>North Mississippi</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Greenbrook</li><li>Goodman Road corridor</li><li>Stateline Road area</li><li>Horn Lake</li><li>Olive Branch</li><li>Hernando</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Southaven is mostly brick-front and vinyl-sided subdivision homes built from the 1980s through the 2000s, with newer construction spreading south and east across DeSoto County.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Feb 1994</b><span>North Mississippi ice storm with heavy tree and power-line damage</span></li><li><b>Feb 2021</b><span>Winter storm and statewide freeze, with burst pipes</span></li><li><b>Dec 2022</b><span>Hard freeze and frozen-pipe losses</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Hail on architectural shingles</li><li>Straight-line wind from spring and summer storms</li><li>Ice storms and tree limb damage</li><li>Frozen pipes during hard freezes</li><li>Siding and gutter damage</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Southaven in DeSoto County</h2>
<p>Southaven sits at the top of the state, just across the line from Memphis, Tennessee, and is one of Mississippi’s largest cities. DeSoto County’s seat is Hernando, a few miles south. Along with Olive Branch and Horn Lake, Southaven has grown into the Mississippi side of the Memphis metro.</p>
<p>Because so many homes here were built in the same era with similar materials, a single storm can damage many similar roofs at once. Carriers often bring in out-of-area adjusters after a large hail event, and their estimates can vary widely from street to street.</p>
<p>Two roads frame much of the city. Stateline Road runs along the northern edge, and Goodman Road carries most of the retail and traffic east and west. Interstate 55 runs through the middle.</p>

<h2>What damages Southaven homes</h2>
<p>Southaven doesn’t see hurricanes, but it sees almost everything else:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hail:</strong> spring storms drop hail that bruises and cracks architectural shingles, dents gutters and splits vinyl siding.</li>
<li><strong>Straight-line wind:</strong> severe thunderstorms push wind strong enough to lift shingles, topple fences and drop limbs.</li>
<li><strong>Ice:</strong> the February 1994 ice storm brought down trees and power lines across North Mississippi. The February 2021 winter storm added ice, snow and burst pipes.</li>
<li><strong>Freeze:</strong> the December 2022 hard freeze caught plumbing in attics and outside walls.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The subdivision roof dispute</h2>
<p>Most of Southaven was built between the 1980s and the 2000s, in subdivisions like Greenbrook and the neighborhoods along Goodman Road and Stateline Road. Those homes tend to share the same builder-grade materials. That creates a predictable set of arguments after a hail or wind storm.</p>
<h3>Repair or replace</h3>
<p>Carriers often approve a few slopes or a set number of shingles. If the shingle line is discontinued or the color has faded, a partial repair won’t match. Whether matching is owed depends on your policy, but the cost of a proper repair is the kind of amount dispute appraisal handles.</p>
<h3>Measurements and waste</h3>
<p>Roof square counts, pitch and waste factor drive the whole roof estimate. Short measurements carry through every line. Our <a href="/claim-calculator-suite/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/">roof pitch and squares calculator</a> helps you check the carrier’s numbers.</p>
<h3>Hail on soft metals and siding</h3>
<p>Estimates sometimes include gutters and downspouts but leave off vents, flashing, window wraps or vinyl siding on the storm-facing side.</p>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">Depreciation and holdback</b><p>Many DeSoto County roof claims are paid on an actual cash value basis first, with depreciation held back until the work is done. Track deadlines for recovering that holdback; they are often in your policy.</p></div>

<h2>Getting a fair number</h2>
<p>If your carrier accepts the claim but the estimate doesn’t cover a real repair, we can review it and, where your policy allows, represent you in appraisal. Our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">roof and hail claim appraisal</a> service is built around exactly these subdivision roof disputes.</p>
<p>We work across DeSoto County, including Olive Branch, Horn Lake and Hernando. Confirm any filing deadline with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Southaven</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Southaven and the rest of DeSoto County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Southaven claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>My carrier will only replace part of my Southaven roof. Is that appraisal?</summary><p>It can be. If the carrier accepts that hail or wind damaged the roof but disagrees on how much repair is needed or what it costs, that is an amount-of-loss dispute. Whether matching is required depends on your policy language.</p></details><details><summary>Do you serve Olive Branch, Horn Lake and Hernando?</summary><p>Yes. We work claims throughout DeSoto County and the rest of Mississippi.</p></details></div>
